<mxfile host="drawio" version="26.0.0">
  <diagram name="Cyberdeck-Starter">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1800" pageHeight="1400" math="0" shadow="0" background="#07090f">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="title" value="CYBERDECK — draw.io starter&#xa;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:15px;color:#7f8ea3&quot;&gt;copy the primitives below. delete this page&#39;s legend when you&#39;re done.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Menlo;fontSize=28;fontColor=#27d4ff;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="40" width="1100" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="rules" value="NON-NEGOTIABLE&#xa;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:13px;color:#8fa3bf&quot;&gt;1. The canvas is ALWAYS dark. This file sets&#xa;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;mxGraphModel background=&quot;#07090f&quot;. Never clear it,&#xa;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;never set it to none — &quot;none&quot; renders WHITE.&#xa;&#xa;2. Every labelled edge needs labelBackgroundColor=#07090f.&#xa;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;draw.io defaults edge labels to a WHITE box.&#xa;&#xa;3. Edges must be light. Default black vanishes here.&#xa;&#xa;4. Colour never carries meaning alone — every coloured&#xa;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;group also gets a text label or a number.&#xa;&#xa;5. Font is Menlo, and big. 15px floor on body text.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0a0d15;strokeColor=#ff4f4f;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#ff4f4f;fontFamily=Menlo;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingTop=12" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="160" width="520" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="palhdr" value="PALETTE" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontFamily=Menlo;fontSize=17;fontColor=#27d4ff;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="160" width="300" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
